<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Carib War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1795–1797</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Carib War was fought on Saint Vincent from 1795 to 1797 between the British and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garifuna">Garifuna</a>, or Black Caribs, who were encouraged by revolutionary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Led at first by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-chatoyer">Joseph Chatoyer</a>, who was killed in March 1795, the Garifuna and their French allies overran much of the island. After their surrender in 1796, the British deported most Garifuna, first to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balliceaux">Balliceaux</a> and then to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roatan">Roatán</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-carib-war.jpg" alt="Second Carib War" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Jeffreys · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Carib_Land_after_Treaty_of_1773.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
